"dogscoff" <dogscoff@eudoramail.com> writes:

> Wandering about Dlvl2 as an XPlvl1 wizard, when I get
> 
> Your pack shakes violently --more--
> You die --more--
> DYWYPI?
> 
> My tombstone reads "Killed by violence"
> 
> Now I happen to know that the "pack shakes violently" message is
> associated with magic traps, so i 'm guessing some magic trap effect
> knocked off my last few points of HP (despite my CoMR). However, had I
> been an unspoiled newbie player I think I would be a little narked off
> at this sudden, apparently arbitrary and totally unexplained end to my
> game. Should this therefore be considered soemthing that needs fixing?

In vanilla Nethack, the "pack shakes violently" message is just a
message with no effect.  In Slash'EM, if you have fixinv turned off,
one-tenth of your items will have their inventory letters randomised.
If you have fixinv turned on (which I think is the default), you will
instead lose 2 HP for each item that would have been randomised.

IMHO, although your death was no more sudden or arbitrary than being
caught in a magical explosion, this is a bad feature because whether
the player has fixinv on or off should not make any difference to the
behaviour of magic traps in the game world.
